Subject: The nursery gate is on when a unit is linked in; chunk hand-out pauses while every cell is promoted

What this does
  - quickjs.c: `qjs_y_gate` starts at 0 and is set when the runtime starts with a unit linked in (`qjs_aot_count > 0`). QJS_Y_GATE=0/1 in the environment still fixes it either way.
  - quickjs.c: over each window of 32768 cells the refill counts the cells that left the nursery as ordinary objects; when 98 in 100 did (a program that builds a long-lived structure), it hands out no chunk for 2^20 requests (the caller makes a counted object per refused request) and the gate drops; the next window is measured afresh.

Why we need it
  With the gate on in an interpreter-only run the reconcile was paced by allocation pressure for a program with no compiled code, and the interpreter ran splay at half its speed. Compiled code needs the gate (raytrace: 5200 without it, 8300 with it). A program that promotes every cell it makes (splay) gains nothing from the nursery and pays the scan form's reconcile, so the nursery steps aside for a while.

Soundness
  Only the reconcile pacing and the chunk hand-out change; cells already in the nursery are unaffected, and a refused request makes the caller's ordinary counted allocation.

Failure modes
  A program that builds a long-lived structure and then turns to short-lived work sees the nursery paused for up to 2^20 requests.

Tests
  Interpreter-only Octane splay at its earlier score; the splay and earleyboyer units run to a score with their checks.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -4659,7 +4659,11 @@
           y_roots[y_roots_n++] = p; y_roots_cap = y_roots_n; return; }
     }
     y_roots_cap = y_roots_cap ? y_roots_cap * 2 : 65536; y_roots = __builtin_realloc(y_roots, (size_t)y_roots_cap * sizeof(void *)); y_roots[y_roots_n++] = p; }
-int qjs_y_force, qjs_y_gate = 1;
+/* Whether reconciles are paced by allocation pressure alone, because compiled code allocates (nursery cells never reach the zero-count table, and
+   the scan form leaves the deaths to the reconcile). It is on when a unit is linked in, so an interpreter-only run keeps the count-paced
+   reconcile; QJS_Y_GATE=0/1 in the environment fixes it either way. */
+int qjs_y_force, qjs_y_gate = 0;
+static int y_gate_fixed;
 static uint64_t y_cyc[8], y_cnt[16], y_pinr, y_pinv;
 uint64_t qjs_y_ep48 = (uint64_t)1 << 48; static uint32_t y_epoch = 1;
